From: FlipperOneEmu
Subject: [PATCH] accel/tcg: broadcast TLB maintenance without stopping every CPU

A broadcast flush (tlb_flush_*_all_cpus_synced: an Arm TLBI ...IS) ran
as an exclusive section. The source left its execution loop, every other
CPU was kicked out of its own and the halted ones woken (each taking the
BQL to process its work), the MCU's cores too, and all waited until the
source had flushed itself. Linux on the RK3576's ARMv8.0 cores issues one
at each copy-on-write fault and each first write to a clean page: some
290 for each process a shell starts, each holding the source for about
48 us.

Now the source flushes itself, asks the same flush of each other CPU on
its memory, and waits only for those running guest code. They do it
between two TBs, without leaving cpu_exec or taking the BQL. A CPU not
running guest code does it before it next runs some, so it is neither
woken nor waited for. While it waits, the source does what is asked of
it, so that two sources never wait for each other. A CPU that does not
answer within 50 us (blocked for the BQL, or its thread not scheduled)
makes the source fall back to the exclusive section.

---
--- a/include/hw/core/cpu.h	2026-11-27 16:49:52.909191764 -0500
+++ b/include/hw/core/cpu.h	2026-11-27 16:51:12.868547061 -0500
@@ -316,6 +316,27 @@
     size_t full_flush_count;
     size_t part_flush_count;
     size_t elide_flush_count;
+    /*
+     * The flushes that other CPUs' broadcast maintenance has asked of this
+     * one (tlb_flush_*_all_cpus_synced), which it does itself: between two
+     * TBs, or before it next runs guest code (see tlb_shootdown()).
+     * @req_lock guards the queue (a request of @req_len 0 is a page's;
+     * past its end, or for a whole flush, the mmu_idxes of @req_full);
+     * @req_gen counts the requests, @req_done those done (atomically, with
+     * release), and @req_pending is set while some wait.
+     */
+    QemuSpin req_lock;
+    bool req_pending;
+    MMUIdxMap req_full;
+    uint32_t req_n;
+    struct {
+        vaddr addr;
+        vaddr len;
+        MMUIdxMap idxmap;
+        unsigned bits;
+    } req[16];
+    uint64_t req_gen;
+    uint64_t req_done;
 } CPUTLBCommon;
 
